  "note": "abap2ui5-linter baseline: findings that existed when the linter was adopted. Suppressed on every run; NEW findings still fail, a STALE entry fails too. Regenerate with --update-baseline. Down from 86 to 74: the twelve that went were real defects or deliberate demonstrations, and each was answered in the SOURCE - fixed, or given a disable directive that says why. Of the 74 left, 30 are false findings the pinned linter 0.1.1 still produces and @abap2ui5/linter 0.2.0 no longer does (11 unknown-binding-path, 7 unknown-model, 5 event-without-handler, 4 missing-view-display-on-navigated, 3 missing-accessibility): a nested or INCLUDE-built structure, a type owned by another class, a model a template:repeat declares, a WHEN OTHERS dispatcher, a branch that delegates its view_display, a button labelled by a COND. They all go stale with the pin bump - and a stale entry FAILS, so the bump is what clears them, not a person remembering to. One commercial-ui5-host entry is deliberate: app 449 feeds the PDFViewer a sample PDF hosted only on the SAPUI5 demo kit, and no OpenUI5 equivalent of that asset could be confirmed.",
